meta {
  name: Delete a wallpaper
  type: http
  seq: 7
  tags: [
    owner-or-moderator
    write
  ]
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/wallpapers/{{createdWallpaperId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  ~Accept-Language: de
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 204
}

docs {
  Delete a wallpaper (deleteWallpaper)

  Removes the wallpaper from the catalog and the search index, and frees its media asset for a new wallpaper.
  Author or moderator only.

  A wallpaper that a moderator took down (status `REMOVED`) cannot be deleted by its author: `409`
  (`wallpaper.removed-by-moderation`). Otherwise deleting it would free the asset and the author could simply repost
  the same picture. Only a moderator (or admin) can delete a `REMOVED` wallpaper. A `REJECTED` wallpaper can be
  deleted by its author, so the asset can be used for a corrected submission.

  Access: `owner-or-moderator`.
  Works on `{{createdWallpaperId}}`, which an earlier request of this collection creates, so seed data stays untouched.
  Error codes: `wallpaper.not-found`, `wallpaper.not-owner`, `wallpaper.removed-by-moderation`.
}
